{
  "name": "six nodes on three machines",
  "comments": [
    "Two nodes on each of client-host, server-host and farm-host, so the cluster's links cross a real",
    "network instead of loopback - the cheaper and the less honest of the two arrangements.",
    "",
    "The load is the small point-to-point scenario: publishers on node3 (server-host), subscribers on",
    "node6 (farm-host), so every message in it crosses a machine boundary. node6 is taken away at 40s",
    "and brought back at 70s; the checks then ask whether the cluster is whole again, whether every",
    "machine still serves clients, and whether traffic crosses the hosts.",
    "",
    "Four messages are carried before anything is done to the cluster, written as the four corners of",
    "one question: whether a publication reaches a subscriber on another node, and if not, whether it",
    "is the pair of machines, the direction, or the machine itself. server-host to farm-host; farm-host to",
    "client-host; farm-host to farm-host; farm-host to server-host. A fifth is carried after node6 comes back.",
    "One check in a corner is a curiosity; four of them say what the shape of the failure is.",
    "",
    "They run early and with short timeouts, so that a corner that does not answer cannot push the",
    "rest of the timeline: the node has to be taken away at 40s as the load expects, not once the",
    "checks have run out of patience."
  ],
  "cluster": "node1@client-host node2@client-host node3@server-host node4@server-host node5@farm-host node6@farm-host",
  "server": {
    "username": "user",
    "password": "User-Secret1"
  },
  "load": {
    "scenario": "cluster-p2p-small.json",
    "groups": [
      {
        "name": "publishers",
        "node": "node3"
      },
      {
        "name": "subscribers",
        "node": "node6"
      }
    ]
  },
  "nodes": [
    {
      "name": "node1",
      "host": "client-host",
      "stop": "ssh client-host /home/alexeyp/cluster/test_cluster.sh stop {node}",
      "start": "ssh client-host /home/alexeyp/cluster/test_cluster.sh start {node}"
    },
    {
      "name": "node2",
      "host": "client-host",
      "stop": "ssh client-host /home/alexeyp/cluster/test_cluster.sh stop {node}",
      "start": "ssh client-host /home/alexeyp/cluster/test_cluster.sh start {node}"
    },
    {
      "name": "node3",
      "host": "server-host",
      "stop": "ssh server-host /home/alexeyp/cluster/test_cluster.sh stop {node}",
      "start": "ssh server-host /home/alexeyp/cluster/test_cluster.sh start {node}"
    },
    {
      "name": "node4",
      "host": "server-host",
      "stop": "ssh server-host /home/alexeyp/cluster/test_cluster.sh stop {node}",
      "start": "ssh server-host /home/alexeyp/cluster/test_cluster.sh start {node}"
    },
    {
      "name": "node5",
      "host": "farm-host",
      "stop": "ssh farm-host /home/alexeyp/cluster/test_cluster.sh stop {node}",
      "start": "ssh farm-host /home/alexeyp/cluster/test_cluster.sh start {node}"
    },
    {
      "name": "node6",
      "host": "farm-host",
      "stop": "ssh farm-host /home/alexeyp/cluster/test_cluster.sh stop {node}",
      "start": "ssh farm-host /home/alexeyp/cluster/test_cluster.sh start {node}"
    }
  ],
  "timeline": [
    {
      "at": 10,
      "action": "check",
      "check": "publish on server-host, subscribe on farm-host"
    },
    {
      "at": 14,
      "action": "check",
      "check": "publish on farm-host, subscribe on client-host"
    },
    {
      "at": 18,
      "action": "check",
      "check": "publish on farm-host, subscribe on farm-host"
    },
    {
      "at": 22,
      "action": "check",
      "check": "publish on farm-host, subscribe on server-host"
    },
    {
      "at": 40,
      "action": "stop",
      "node": "node6"
    },
    {
      "at": 70,
      "action": "start",
      "node": "node6"
    },
    {
      "at": 100,
      "action": "check"
    }
  ],
  "checks": [
    {
      "name": "all six nodes are members",
      "kind": "redis",
      "uri": "redis://farm-host:6379/4",
      "command": "ZCARD cluster:members",
      "expect": "6"
    },
    {
      "name": "a coordinator is leading",
      "kind": "redis",
      "uri": "redis://farm-host:6379/4",
      "command": "GET cluster:coordinator",
      "nonempty": true
    },
    {
      "name": "client-host serves clients",
      "kind": "mqtt",
      "action": "connect",
      "node": "node1",
      "expect": true
    },
    {
      "name": "server-host serves clients",
      "kind": "mqtt",
      "action": "connect",
      "node": "node3",
      "expect": true
    },
    {
      "name": "farm-host serves clients",
      "kind": "mqtt",
      "action": "connect",
      "node": "node5",
      "expect": true
    },
    {
      "name": "the node that was away serves clients again",
      "kind": "mqtt",
      "action": "connect",
      "node": "node6",
      "expect": true
    },
    {
      "name": "publish on server-host, subscribe on farm-host",
      "kind": "mqtt",
      "action": "deliver",
      "publish-node": "node3",
      "subscribe-node": "node6",
      "topic": "cluster/test/server-host-to-farm-host",
      "payload": "server-host-to-farm-host",
      "timeout": 5,
      "settle": 3
    },
    {
      "name": "publish on farm-host, subscribe on client-host",
      "kind": "mqtt",
      "action": "deliver",
      "publish-node": "node5",
      "subscribe-node": "node1",
      "topic": "cluster/test/farm-host-to-client-host",
      "payload": "farm-host-to-client-host",
      "timeout": 5,
      "settle": 3
    },
    {
      "name": "publish on farm-host, subscribe on farm-host",
      "kind": "mqtt",
      "action": "deliver",
      "publish-node": "node5",
      "subscribe-node": "node6",
      "topic": "cluster/test/farm-host-to-farm-host",
      "payload": "farm-host-to-farm-host",
      "timeout": 5,
      "settle": 3
    },
    {
      "name": "publish on farm-host, subscribe on server-host",
      "kind": "mqtt",
      "action": "deliver",
      "publish-node": "node6",
      "subscribe-node": "node3",
      "topic": "cluster/test/farm-host-to-server-host",
      "payload": "farm-host-to-server-host",
      "timeout": 5,
      "settle": 3
    },
    {
      "name": "publish on server-host, subscribe on farm-host after the restart",
      "kind": "mqtt",
      "action": "deliver",
      "publish-node": "node3",
      "subscribe-node": "node6",
      "topic": "cluster/test/after-the-restart",
      "payload": "after-the-restart",
      "timeout": 15,
      "settle": 3
    },
    {
      "name": "a retained message crosses the machines",
      "kind": "mqtt",
      "action": "retained",
      "publish-node": "node5",
      "subscribe-node": "node1",
      "topic": "cluster/test/retained-across-machines",
      "payload": "retained-across",
      "timeout": 15
    }
  ],
  "before": [
    "~/cluster/test_cluster.sh mark"
  ],
  "after": [
    "~/cluster/test_cluster.sh check-logs"
  ]
}
